+## Optional hadronic interactions
+
+Charged-pion and proton inelastic interactions can be enabled with an external
+calibration table. The runtime is independent of Geant4; the table-generation
+and calibration workflow belongs outside ACTS. See @ref fatras_hadronic for the
+model, file format, supported domain and validation requirements.
+
+In C++, set `FatrasSimulation::Config::nuclearInteractionTable` to the table path.
+An empty path preserves the EM-only configuration. The Python helper accepts the
+same option:
+
+```python
+addFatras(
+    sequencer, trackingGeometry, field, randomNumbers,
+    pMin=0.1 * acts.UnitConstants.GeV,
+    pTMin=0.05 * acts.UnitConstants.GeV,
+    nuclearInteractionTable="charged-hadrons.table",
+)
+```
+
+These cuts are illustrative, not tuned defaults. `pMin` applies to all input and
+secondary particles; `pTMin` applies only to charged particles and is also checked
+during transport. `enableInteractions=False` disables the hadronic model along
+with the EM processes. Supplying an unreadable or invalid table fails algorithm
+construction. Unsupported table regions do not generate nuclear interactions,
+so material and momentum coverage must be validated for the intended detector.
+
 ## Barcode identifiers {#fatras_barcode_identifiers}
 
 Fatras labels simulated particles and hits with @ref ActsFatras::Barcode. A
